    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 223,
        "text": "Welcome, everyone. Today we're looking at how public claims are evaluated when the evidence is uncertain. Let's start with a claim that was made last month: 'The new park will reduce city temperatures by two degrees.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "a115a3e256cbf775e919160881e8fabca64d36425a9ddab5ac85c47270f11a48",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 230,
        "sourceEnd": 299,
        "text": "Sorry, can I just check — was that two degrees Celsius or Fahrenheit?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "6b43ca1d52d9bad41a02dddfd1ebc816639ce11a7c886121a94a6209909fddac",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 307,
        "sourceEnd": 435,
        "text": "Good question. The original report said two degrees Celsius, but it was later corrected to one degree. So the claim was revised.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "74c486ad6f90ed5055ccb357d7177f7c8cefea543cbdfe5ab6a1acfdcff5b80a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 442,
        "sourceEnd": 499,
        "text": "Right. And was the measurement taken in summer or winter?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "0c3fcaa9fc40c17632a924de3c2fe53c63b1c140d1110b96d0220a31345b014d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 507,
        "sourceEnd": 598,
        "text": "It was taken in summer, over three weeks. But the sample was small — only one neighborhood.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "d825bbf05e7f2eba3cf9ba944532598b15210b91b39632ebc2e27908c1dbd7c1",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 605,
        "sourceEnd": 659,
        "text": "So the claim is uncertain because the data is limited.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a3601b3caf16f9bc016e11667e26c93a57d0f40a5ae103fe0a2dd8f0f7e89b10",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 667,
        "sourceEnd": 779,
        "text": "Exactly. Now, how should we present this to the public? We need to be clear about what is known and what is not.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "5a0dbfee6456702135690016fbe1b04ccb50c72568fcc6bc39e71009abb7500f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 786,
        "sourceEnd": 881,
        "text": "I think we should say: 'Early results suggest a small cooling effect, but more data is needed.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "8ab339e06f90ca506a584f2406f8a4de615bca83c4f509d4636c83b51599ebd5",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 889,
        "sourceEnd": 1018,
        "text": "That's better. It avoids overclaiming. Now let's look at the second claim: 'The new bus route has reduced traffic by 30 percent.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "4777609eca7ee7e19a3bacd90020cb38e6c9c65679fa76ae1b3f68389a4b08b0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1025,
        "sourceEnd": 1077,
        "text": "Was that measured before and after the route opened?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "ef48390d5ea8faa3a27129a5d712fc6d9c8d9a11b10f2fce99ac4c598cc69c96",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1085,
        "sourceEnd": 1194,
        "text": "Yes, but only on one road. And the measurement was taken during a holiday period, so traffic was already low.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "797a14167e85ab08aa3e89edf04dba0fd09208067c8dd74eb35f648106da7e23",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1201,
        "sourceEnd": 1246,
        "text": "So the 30 percent figure might be misleading.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "f405b6116ec0a2b27d5866d3b30d52b6760a66b094efa6b16ae7d521519649a8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1254,
        "sourceEnd": 1412,
        "text": "Correct. The claim was based on a short period and a single location. Now, what about the third claim: 'The library will be closed for renovation next month.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "74b1a5f767a300337db5a6aaf93ad235042a7fbfac79d9bc83a99d8e878dd173",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1419,
        "sourceEnd": 1476,
        "text": "That one seems clear. Was there an official announcement?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "b9c0a5dfca41ef544f2a8d57c9dffe1c65fc6ea2d20efefc778068d0eab76c40",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1484,
        "sourceEnd": 1555,
        "text": "Yes, the city council announced it. But the exact dates were not given.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "81575dafd953786c839fb806261923661ba7b44292746f39f744cdca794c2fb8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1562,
        "sourceEnd": 1615,
        "text": "So the claim is true, but the details are incomplete.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "9eb4e8f67ada9206e67f1a341e5d06209ff79f1cd75ad2fb187f343c191715eb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1623,
        "sourceEnd": 1787,
        "text": "Right. Now, let's think about how to communicate uncertainty. We can use phrases like 'it is likely that', 'the evidence suggests', or 'further research is needed'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "afe8f72399008fe7b540a1c9c388362d603f305feb9095711b1f3c4970ddc5a2",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 1794,
        "sourceEnd": 1850,
        "text": "And we should avoid saying 'it is proven' when it isn't.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "12a98603b82f5998867fbe5d078229317be8f65613db27b8a20c48fbd98b77cc",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1858,
        "sourceEnd": 2028,
        "text": "Exactly. Also, when we describe a process, we should use the passive voice to focus on the action, not the person. For example: 'The data was collected over three weeks.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "611e982474276346d7e3a88f92926ae8b56d050ca8b096039d15b85a58d4e3bb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2035,
        "sourceEnd": 2113,
        "text": "And for sequences, we use words like 'first', 'then', 'after that', 'finally'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "a7a6bc8df08395f07f996c2599d2eea20bb75fb8d4786d19a59931ca055882ea",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2121,
        "sourceEnd": 2252,
        "text": "Yes. And for changes, we can say 'the temperature increased by one degree' or 'traffic decreased from 100 to 70 vehicles per hour'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "8db2666ea63350410be85f1a29f6b6ae31512bf06c5f96a1a9ce7de3bdd0ed30",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2259,
        "sourceEnd": 2352,
        "text": "What about linking ideas between sentences? We can use 'however', 'therefore', 'in addition'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "4c214d07737e81553b405f7b1d1d29d9fe5c95443b6efaf513d7a9cf63e7e672",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2360,
        "sourceEnd": 2488,
        "text": "Good. Now, let's practice with a short example. Imagine a claim: 'The new lighting in the park has reduced crime by 15 percent.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "4bfe9e1dc0eb621f70ff2f9f69b46f48df5d628b086832aaf33df7bc7fdc9f56",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2495,
        "sourceEnd": 2530,
        "text": "Was that measured over a full year?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "0ed35ae1efa027cf65ffb47d63fea5ab605371276eb052e7ca4aa0f34aadaf9b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2538,
        "sourceEnd": 2598,
        "text": "No, only six months. And the police reports were incomplete.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "02ff0d68565275fba0fdd164f8467407adba0c85473c9880df631f46e4b92596",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2605,
        "sourceEnd": 2721,
        "text": "So the claim is uncertain. We should say: 'Initial data suggests a possible reduction, but the evidence is limited.'",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "18434cbbfe17f66c0033821ca4bce3ffce00da6fa1a6dc4633f3d5bfe7ddc2c4",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2729,
        "sourceEnd": 2912,
        "text": "Perfect. Now, let's review the key points. First, check the source of the data. Second, check the time period. Third, check the location. Finally, check if the claim has been revised.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "2eb6e61561d2cbc5b4c091a39c84673c09b7bc5d42ee8a82d9e35764ae9443d8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "ben",
        "speaker": "Ben",
        "sourceStart": 2919,
        "sourceEnd": 2983,
        "text": "And always use cautious language when the evidence is uncertain.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "b79e85a50e36d73027c914d892db13bc1955c6bd7f88ee71187b3e1e399b9539",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 2991,
        "sourceEnd": 3032,
        "text": "Exactly. That's all for today. Thank you.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "e726e716a461dfdd358eef40ea82f990c0b0402cbd0365beef488a88cfe4952f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
